# Intent: Safety fix. The public CA bundle (66,137 B of flash, about 140 roots) is replaced by a custom bundle that holds one placeholder root whose key was destroyed, so nothing can chain to it. The core needs no public root: the unit talks to the host over the private network only, and the TLS link to the host (a later item) pins a private CA that is added to firmware/ca/ then. The Kconfig switches ride in firmware/sdkconfig.core.defaults.
# Placement: unit (the unit's trust store)
# Upstream: none (new file)
# Check after a flash: nothing visible; any https connection to a public site now fails with a certificate error, which is intended.
diff --git a/firmware/ca/no-public-roots.pem b/firmware/ca/no-public-roots.pem
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
